# The gallery thumbnails are a DERIVED OUTPUT, not a source.
#
# `reports/HTML/make_gallery.py` copies six samples of every type from the dataset into
# this folder (`copy_thumbnails()`), and `reports/HTML/index.html` refers to them by the
# relative path `img/t/<type>/<file>.png`.
#
# The dataset pictures themselves are NOT in this repository (ADR 0004: the dataset lives on
# Hugging Face). A copy of dataset pictures inside the repository is therefore a duplicate
# of a payload the repository has already decided not to carry, so these files are excluded
# from git the same way `dataset/out/**/*.png` is.
#
# They stay on the machine of the owner, so `reports/HTML/index.html` opens with the full
# gallery there. To restore them in a fresh clone, take them from the git history:
#
#     git log --diff-filter=D --name-only -- reports/HTML/img/t | head
#     git checkout <commit>^ -- reports/HTML/img/t
#
# Measured on 2026-10-27: of the 276 pictures, 46 (the `001.png` of every type) are byte-identical
# to the showcase `dataset/samples/<type>/001.png`, which stays in git; the other **230 are unique**
# — they are samples of the old 46-type render, which is neither on disk nor on Hugging Face any
# more (HF holds the new 20-type render in parquet). The git history is therefore the last copy of
# them: keep that in mind before cleaning the history.
#
# The rule belongs to the root `.gitignore` as well (that file is owned by the main agent);
# this nested copy makes the exclusion work without it.
#
# 2026-10-27 — cleanup of `reports/`
*.png
